#!/usr/bin/env -S da run
# kg-ingest.da — mechanical KG ingestion of a FOLDER TREE, dynamic across source types.
#
# Ingests every supported file anywhere under a folder into the local knowledge
# graph and materializes the notes into the warm query layer. Run this to warm the
# KG before an inner-loop session so kg-brief / kg-ideate query fresh content
# instead of degrading to "no prior decisions".
#
# Recursive + dynamic-by-source: one type-scoped `for … in <base>/**/<glob>` loop
# per source kind. The `**` segment matches the base and every descendant at any
# depth, so a single run ingests a whole TREE of mixed types — each file gets the
# right --type, and a type with no files is a clean no-op (empty match → zero
# iterations). Uses the mechanical control flow from da-recipe-scripts §8 (recursive
# loops + the `if set` guard; nesting depth cap = 2, honored here as if→for).
#
# Env vars:
#   KG_DIR   folder tree to ingest (required). The whole body is guarded by
#            `if set KG_DIR`, so an unset KG_DIR is a TRUE no-op — nothing ingests,
#            warm doesn't run, and the glob never walks the filesystem ROOT. Set it
#            and everything below runs.
#
# Scope: this recipe ends at `kg warm` on purpose. Rebuilding FTS/flows/communities
# is `kg postprocess`, part of the CODE-graph pipeline — it shells out to the
# code-review-graph toolchain and hard-fails when that toolchain isn't runnable.
# Keeping it out makes this recipe portable (exit 0 everywhere). Get code-graph
# derived data via `da kg build` / `da kg update` (they auto-postprocess) where the
# toolchain is installed; full FTS note-query is gated on that same toolchain.
#
# Not extension-mapped here (url | transcript | meeting_notes | repo_doc): ingest a
# single such source with an explicit type, e.g.
#   da kg ingest <file-or-url> --type transcript --title "<title>"
# then run `da kg warm`. Mixed-inbox batch: queue sources, then `da kg ingest --all`.
#
# Paths are quoted ("${F}") so tree entries with spaces stay one token (expansion is
# quote-blind and runs before tokenization; keep paths free of literal ").
#
# Requires `da run` (0.5.0+; the 0.4.2 binary lacks it — devs: `go run ./cmd/da run
# .agents/recipes/kg-ingest.da`). Directly executable when chmod +x.
if set KG_DIR
  for F in ${KG_DIR}/**/*.md
    kg ingest "${F}" --type markdown
  end
  for F in ${KG_DIR}/**/*.markdown
    kg ingest "${F}" --type markdown
  end
  for F in ${KG_DIR}/**/*.txt
    kg ingest "${F}" --type text
  end
  for F in ${KG_DIR}/**/*.pdf
    kg ingest "${F}" --type pdf
  end
  kg warm
end
